From 5026a01822ce78522959fcbda362344900ec48ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mechres <164776284+Mechres@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 07:11:36 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 05/11] sunxi system layer: T8E power-up with an
 active-power-management split

From the TI 1.17 port's sunxi layer (raw CCU power-up replayed from the stock
driver, no TI OCP wrapper, 300 MHz core clock). EnableSystemClocks brings up the
rail, PRCM and PLLs once; EnableSGXClocks/DisableSGXClocks release/assert the
reset and open/close the gates in the stock order, since active power
management cycles them and SGXInitialise runs again after each power-up. The
register window size comes from the DT resource.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
